<%# End-to-end check that the Opina embed credential never travels in a URL.
    `opina_url` points back at this same app, so the frame is same-origin and the
    `postMessage` is really delivered — `pages#feedback_embed` is the stand-in for
    Opina's embed page and prints whatever token it was handed. %>
<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold p-6">FeedbackWidget — the token arrives by message, not by URL</h1>

<p class="px-6 pb-6 max-w-prose">
  Open the widget with the floating button. The frame's <code>src</code> carries no
  <code>token</code> parameter; the controller hands the token over once the frame
  has loaded, addressed to that frame's exact origin.
</p>

<%= render Bali::FeedbackWidget::Component.new(
  project_slug: 'demo-project',
  opina_url: @opina_url,
  token: 'demo-token-123',
  badge_interval: 0
) %>
